{
  "requirement": "The SDK exposes continuation operations for prepared node and source results\nthrough its fixed `get_node_page` and `get_source_page` agent tools. Each accepts\na page ID issued with a prepared tool result and returns the corresponding page.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has two obligations. The SDK must expose fixed `get_node_page` and `get_source_page` tools. Each tool must accept a page ID issued with a prepared result and return the corresponding page. The reviewed tests cover both.\n\n**Node pages**\n- `application_tools_preserve_graph_tools_in_the_same_conversation` (`agent/tests.rs`) checks that every request's tool list includes `get_node_page` next to `read_node`.\n- In the same test, the scripted provider (`Script`'s `CompletionProvider::complete`) replaces the `prepared_page` index with the real page ID from the `read_node` result. It does this through the helper `returned_node_page`.\n- The test then asserts that the `get_node_page` delivery is exactly `{\"page\": <ID of page 1>, \"text\": \"x\" * 8192}`. That is the page the issued ID refers to.\n- `graph_read_pages_retain_the_prepared_snapshot_after_contents_change` also fetches a page by its issued ID. It asserts that the page text comes from the original snapshot.\n\n**Source pages**\n- `fixed_tools_deliver_domain_contents_with_mandatory_snapshot_dependencies` (`agent/project_sources.rs`) asserts that the fixed tool list ends with `get_source_page`.\n- The same test dispatches `get_source_page` with each page ID from a `read_source` envelope. It asserts that the pages concatenate to the full 20,000-character text and that the dependencies are preserved.\n- It also checks that an unknown page ID (999999), page 0 on a fresh session, and a page ID issued to a different session are all rejected.\n- `source_read_pages_retain_text_and_dependencies_without_another_read` fetches every issued page. It reassembles the complete JSON result and compares it to the original text, so each page is the correct one.\n\nI found no obligation of the subject without a test, and no assertion that contradicts it.",
